    "q-98638": {
      "dom_id": "step-q98638",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrix $V?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=6$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=36,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-36I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 36\\end{aligned}]-36[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-36 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-36I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 36\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 36\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrix $V:$\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-98638-a",
